{"_id":"bBYlGimrmNuNOM22","name":"Tug","type":"ship","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"health":{"value":10,"min":0,"max":10,"label":"Health"},"hits":{"value":0,"min":0,"max":2,"label":"Wounds"},"netHP":{"value":10,"min":0,"max":10,"label":"Net HP"},"bleeding":{"value":0,"min":0,"label":"Bleeding"},"biography":"<h3>Deckplan</h3><ol><li><strong>Airlock.</strong> Main entry.</li><li><strong>Command and Habitat.</strong> Small piloting deck.</li><li><strong>Cryochamber.</strong> With four cryopods.</li><li><strong>Life Support and Engineering.</strong> O2 and utilities.</li><li><strong>Reactor.</strong> Mini-nuke reactor suitable for small craft. Level 1 (trace) Radiation.</li></ol>","description":"<p>Tugs are small, inter-system craft used to tow large ships into ports. They have frequently been retrofitted to a number of purposes, including piracy and smuggling. Their diminutive size means they rely on the element of surprise. Standard Tugs cannot make Jumps, although they can be upgraded with Jump drives.</p><p><strong>Installed:</strong> Magnetic Towing Clamps.</p><p><strong>Note:</strong> This ship must have a weapon installed to deal 1 MDMG.</p>","type":"Inter-system Craft","class":"Tug","runSetup":false,"images":{"layout":"systems/mosh/images/Galloway_Top.png","beauty":"systems/mosh/images/Galloway_Top.png"},"xp":{"value":1},"stats":{"thrusters":{"value":25,"min":0,"max":99,"label":"Thrusters","rollLabel":"Thrusters Save"},"battle":{"value":5,"min":0,"max":99,"label":"Battle","rollLabel":"Battle Save"},"systems":{"value":15,"min":0,"max":99,"label":"Systems","rollLabel":"Systems Save"},"armor":{"value":0,"min":0,"max":99,"label":"Armor","rollLabel":"Armor Save"},"speed":{"value":25,"min":0,"max":99,"label":"Speed","rollLabel":"Speed Check"},"intellect":{"value":15,"min":0,"max":99,"label":"Intellect","rollLabel":"Intellect Check"},"combat":{"value":5,"min":0,"max":99,"label":"Combat","rollLabel":"Combat Check"},"bankruptcy":{"value":10,"min":0,"max":99